          '`tests/e2e/hotel-upper.spec.js` on the same URL (lift waits use `{ timeout: 40000 }` because lift time is game time and software WebGL runs it slowly): test 1 lift to the roof: teleport `(-4.8, -0.4, 4.0, -1.5708)` (first floor, west of the call button, facing east), `useNearest()` (it is `plaza:lift1-call-1`), poll `liftState("plaza:lift1")` `state` `open` with `currentFloor` 1; teleport `(-2.8, -1.5, 4.0, -1.5708)` (inside the cabin in front of the third button), `useNearest()` (it is `plaza:lift1-btn-2`), sample `playerState().y` every 300 ms into an array until `liftState` is `open` with `currentFloor` 2: the final y is within 0.1 of 7.8, the samples never decrease and at least two lie between 4.3 and 7.5. Test 2 roof walk: teleport `(-4.8, -2.0, 7.8, 1.5708)` (roof, west of the lift front, facing west), hold `w` and poll until `playerState().x` is at most -7.8 while every sampled `y` stays within 0.1 of 7.8 (the player walks at least 3 m). Test 3 parapet: teleport `(-4.0, -6.0, 7.8, 0)` (facing north), hold `w` and poll until `playerState().z` is at most -8.5 (moved at least 2.5 m toward the edge), then keep holding for three more polls: every sampled `z` stays at least -9.65 (inside the footprint, the parapet blocks), every `y` within 0.1 of 7.8. Zero console errors.',
