          '`tests/e2e/terrain.spec.js` (every URL has `&time=0.4&freeze=1`; every test collects `console` errors and `pageerror` and asserts none, which also catches a shader compile error; no fixed waits). Test 1, for each tier in `low`, `medium`, `high` (separate page loads of `/?quality=<tier>&time=0.4&freeze=1`, `high` is mandatory because only it compiles the rock-normal shader): wait for `window.__world.ready`; `terrainStats().tier` equals the tier; `canvasLooksRendered`; remember `terrainStats().triangles`; after the three loads `low < medium < high`. Test 2 (`?quality=high`): read the triangles, call `setQuality("low")`, then `expect.poll(() => terrainStats().triangles, { timeout: 15000 })` equals the low value of test 1 (the rebuild on tier change works) and `terrainHeight(10, 10)` is unchanged by the rebuild. Test 3: spawn on the ground: read `playerState()` after ready; with `th = terrainHeight(x, z)` assert `y >= th - 0.1` and `y <= th + 0.6` (the player may stand on a floor slab such as paving or a building floor later, never inside the ground or floating), then `teleport("forge")` and poll until `y` is within `[th - 0.1, th + 0.6]` for the new position.',
